# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# One entry, and it is not ours. SDL_Init(SDL_INIT_VIDEO) enumerates DRM devices, which makes
# libdrm allocate a few small blocks in drmModeObjectGetProperties that it never frees. libdrm is
# not built with LeakSanitizer, so the report has no caller frame above it and there is nothing in
# this repository to fix.
#
# Scoped to the FUNCTION rather than to the library: a leak anywhere else -- including any leak in
# this project's own code -- still fails the gate. This is a much narrower instrument than a
# library-wide suppression, which is why it was acceptable here when the same idea was rejected for
# ThreadSanitizer (a race suppression there would have hidden races between our code and the driver).
leak:drmModeObjectGetProperties
